2025-05-01 01:56:37 - Thread-585 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• “BLOCK_TIMESTAMP”: filter events since Jan‑01‑2023.  
• “ARGS”: contains decoded event parameters (for a Transfer event → index 0 = from, index 1 = to).  
• “EVENT_SIGNATURE”: let us keep only Transfer events.  
• “BLOCK_NUMBER”: we do not have block *size* in these tables; we can still show how to add a numeric‑block filter if needed.  
• “ADDRESS”: contract that emitted the event (not the sender of the tx).  
• “TRANSACTION_HASH” & “LOG_INDEX”: allow de‑duplication.  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (each returns ≤ 20 rows) that progressively drill down to “the most‑frequent sender address” on the chain, while keeping to the columns available in the supplied tables.

```sql
-- 1. Description: View raw rows to get a feeling for the data layout after 1‑Jan‑2023.
SELECT *
FROM "GOOG_BLOCKCHAIN"."GOOG_BLOCKCHAIN_ARBITRUM_ONE_US"."DECODED_EVENTS"
WHERE "BLOCK_TIMESTAMP" >= 1672531200000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: List distinct event signatures observed since 2023.
SELECT DISTINCT "EVENT_SIGNATURE"
FROM "GOOG_BLOCKCHAIN"."GOOG_BLOCKCHAIN_ARBITRUM_ONE_US"."DECODED_EVENTS"
WHERE "BLOCK_TIMESTAMP" >= 1672531200000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Count how many times each event signature occurs (top 20).
SELECT "EVENT_SIGNATURE", COUNT(*) AS "evt_cnt"
FROM "GOOG_BLOCKCHAIN"."GOOG_BLOCKCHAIN_ARBITRUM_ONE_US"."DECODED_EVENTS"
WHERE "BLOCK_TIMESTAMP" >= 1672531200000000
GROUP BY "EVENT_SIGNATURE"
ORDER BY "evt_cnt" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Inspect sample rows of ERC‑20 Transfer events.
SELECT *
FROM "GOOG_BLOCKCHAIN"."GOOG_BLOCKCHAIN_ARBITRUM_ONE_US"."DECODED_EVENTS"
WHERE "BLOCK_TIMESTAMP" >= 1672531200000000
  AND "EVENT_SIGNATURE" = 'Transfer(address,address,uint256)'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Peek inside the JSON‑array held in “ARGS” for Transfer events.
SELECT "ARGS" AS "raw_args"
FROM "GOOG_BLOCKCHAIN"."GOOG_BLOCKCHAIN_ARBITRUM_ONE_US"."DECODED_EVENTS"
WHERE "EVENT_SIGNATURE" = 'Transfer(address,address,uint256)'
  AND "BLOCK_TIMESTAMP" >= 1672531200000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Decode “from” and “to” addresses (index 0 & 1 in ARGS array).
SELECT
  PARSE_JSON("ARGS")[0]::STRING  AS "from_address",
  PARSE_JSON("ARGS")[1]::STRING  AS "to_address",
  "TRANSACTION_HASH",
  "BLOCK_NUMBER"
FROM "GOOG_BLOCKCHAIN"."GOOG_BLOCKCHAIN_ARBITRUM_ONE_US"."DECODED_EVENTS"
WHERE "EVENT_SIGNATURE" = 'Transfer(address,address,uint256)'
  AND "BLOCK_TIMESTAMP" >= 1672531200000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Keep only rows whose “to_address” is not null / not all‑zero.
SELECT
  PARSE_JSON("ARGS")[0]::STRING  AS "from_address",
  PARSE_JSON("ARGS")[1]::STRING  AS "to_address"
FROM "GOOG_BLOCKCHAIN"."GOOG_BLOCKCHAIN_ARBITRUM_ONE_US"."DECODED_EVENTS"
WHERE "EVENT_SIGNATURE" = 'Transfer(address,address,uint256)'
  AND "BLOCK_TIMESTAMP" >= 1672531200000000
  AND PARSE_JSON("ARGS")[1] IS NOT NULL
  AND PARSE_JSON("ARGS")[1]::STRING <> '0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000000'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Aggregate senders (“from_address”) by count, still limited to 2023+.
SELECT
  PARSE_JSON("ARGS")[0]::STRING AS "from_address",
  COUNT(*)                     AS "tx_cnt"
FROM "GOOG_BLOCKCHAIN"."GOOG_BLOCKCHAIN_ARBITRUM_ONE_US"."DECODED_EVENTS"
WHERE "EVENT_SIGNATURE" = 'Transfer(address,address,uint256)'
  AND "BLOCK_TIMESTAMP" >= 1672531200000000
  AND PARSE_JSON("ARGS")[1] IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY "from_address"
ORDER BY "tx_cnt" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Same as #8 but add an *example* block‑size placeholder (≥ 4096)
--     even though block size isn’t present; you might replace with real column if available.
SELECT
  PARSE_JSON("ARGS")[0]::STRING AS "from_address",
  COUNT(*)                     AS "tx_cnt"
FROM "GOOG_BLOCKCHAIN"."GOOG_BLOCKCHAIN_ARBITRUM_ONE_US"."DECODED_EVENTS"
WHERE "EVENT_SIGNATURE" = 'Transfer(address,address,uint256)'
  AND "BLOCK_TIMESTAMP" >= 1672531200000000
  AND PARSE_JSON("ARGS")[1] IS NOT NULL
  AND "BLOCK_NUMBER" >= 4096      -- placeholder for a “large block” filter
GROUP BY "from_address"
ORDER BY "tx_cnt" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: Final drill‑down – top sender address formatted as a Cronoscan URL.
SELECT
  CONCAT('https://cronoscan.com/address/', SUBSTR(PARSE_JSON("ARGS")[0]::STRING, 3)) 
      AS "sender_cronoscan_url",
  COUNT(*) AS "tx_cnt"
FROM "GOOG_BLOCKCHAIN"."GOOG_BLOCKCHAIN_ARBITRUM_ONE_US"."DECODED_EVENTS"
WHERE "EVENT_SIGNATURE" = 'Transfer(address,address,uint256)'
  AND "BLOCK_TIMESTAMP" >= 1672531200000000
  AND PARSE_JSON("ARGS")[1] IS NOT NULL
  AND "BLOCK_NUMBER" >= 4096         -- again, a proxy for “larger blocks”
GROUP BY "sender_cronoscan_url"
ORDER BY "tx_cnt" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

These queries walk from basic inspection to selecting the most‑frequent “from” address (sender) and format it as a clickable Cronoscan URL.
